{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Linking related questions: the build design, version 3 (D694, D695; for council review before code)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose A (D694) and narrowed the first version (D695, \"只连数字题\"): a link joins a **newly opened number question** and an **open\n     4\tnumber question it was shown**, in either reading direction; both are asset questions with five-rung ladders and typed bounds. No\n     5\ttheme, event or same-article pair is linked in this version. A chosen link leaves filing alone (D694 (a)). Version 1 of this document\n     6\twas reviewed in council R round 4 (`codex-r4.md`, NOT READY), version 2 in round 5 (`codex-r5.md`, NOT READY); each finding is\n     7\tanswered below (§10).\n     8\t\n     9\t## 0. Versions and entry points\n    10\t\n    11\t- `poc/config/poc-v119.json`: poc-v118 with `matching.engine` `jev-links` and `rejudging.prompt_version` `judging-v8`; nothing else.\n    12\t- `judging-v8.txt` is a byte copy of `judging-v7.txt`; only the code-built dependency block differs (§3). A request with no dependency is\n    13\t  byte-equal under v7 and v8.\n    14\t- `config.ENGINES` gains `jev-links`. Every place that tests `engine == 'jev'` (`round._match`, `scripts/replay.py`,\n    15\t  `parallel_day.ParallelDay`, `budget_replay.py` defaults) treats `jev-links` as Jev; only `round.run` asks the link questions, and only\n    16\t  under `jev-links`. Existing Jev requests are unchanged (`jev.request_for` holds model, state and questions only).\n    17\t- **A store written by poc-v119 opened by poc-v118:** allowed; v118 writes no link, renders a stored link with today's v7 line, and\n    18\t  filing skips it (filing reads the stored kind, not the configuration). A run is meant to keep one configuration; this is the defined\n    19\t  outcome if it does not.\n    20\t- Pins (`tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py`): the v7 pins stay; added: `judging-v8.txt`'s sha (equal to v7's), the two new\n    21\t  question builders' output, judging-v8's schema (equal to v7's), and a request-level control: one ledger with a link rendered under v8\n    22\t  (exact text) and under v7 (today's text), and one without a link, byte-equal under both.\n    23\t\n    24\t## 1. Where selection runs: after matching has settled what opens\n    25\t\n    26\tIn `round.run`, under `jev-links` only, a new step **after the evidence-only second matching call returns and before the `matched`\n    27\tsuccess marker**, on the first call's `checked.outcomes` and lists:\n    28\t1. From `checked.outcomes` take the candidates whose outcome is `new` or `succession`; `identity.batch_plan(handover.candidates,\n    29\t   checked.outcomes)` gives their aliases; one canonical candidate per stored question. A candidate refused or not opened is not asked.\n    30\t2. **Eligible pairs:** the canonical candidate C and each open thesis T on C's list (its search list plus the item's shown questions,\n    31\t   `lists.candidate_lists[C] + shown`, the list its relation questions used), when both are **number questions**: asset kind; a\n    32\t   measure outside `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (C's own key, T's stored key); five rungs whose canonical labels run Strongly bullish to\n    33\t   Strongly bearish or the reverse; a **typed direction** (§5). C's rungs are taken as the writer will store them\n    34\t   (`writing.oriented_like` for a succession, which may reverse the whole ladder with its labels). A pair outside this set is not\n    35\t   asked. Same-article pairs are not asked (D695).\n    36\t3. **Stage 1, one Jev job per C:** state = `candidate_state(C)`; per eligible T the `READS` question (§2) with `thesis_text(T)`.\n    37\t4. **Stage 2, one Jev job per C with a passing stage-1 answer:** the shared state stays `candidate_state(C)`; per such pair one of two\n    38\t   sign questions, chosen by the stage-1 direction, each naming in its own instructions which question reads which (§2). One job can\n    39\t   hold both directions.\n    40\t5. **The graph check** (§4) on the whole proposed set of the article (every opening candidate's links) plus the stored reading\n    41\t   relation; candidates are represented by their canonical ids until written.\n    42\t6. The selection is recorded in a **new table `link_selections`** (seq, input_id, config checksum, record_json: every pair shown with\n    43\t   its eligibility, each Jev call's call id and request sha, every answer's choice and probabilities, each correction, the links\n    44\t   proposed with direction and sign, and, if a call failed, what had been answered before it). It is not a `match_records` row, so\n    45\t   preflight and the trace grouping (which read `call_no`) are untouched; its readers are the July test and the tests that pin its\n    46\t   shape. The **committed** links are the `dependencies` rows (with the final label computed in the write); a proposed link that the\n    47\t   write does not commit is listed in the article's `written` notes and in `link_selections` (the write appends its outcome there).\n    48\t7. `writing.write` gains a keyword-only argument `proposed_links=None` (today's six-argument callers unchanged), carrying the canonical\n    49\t   endpoints, direction and sign; the write resolves C's new id, computes the label from the stored rungs and writes (§4).\n    50\t\n    51\t`jev.ask` failures (transport or answer shape) fail the article at the step `matched` as a matching failure does today: resumable, and\n    52\ta resume re-asks only what the archive lacks.\n    53\t\n    54\t## 2. The two questions\n    55\t\n    56\t```\n    57\tREADS (choice), state = CANDIDATE (candidate_state), per THESIS:\n    58\t instructions: \"Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text(T)\n    59\t \"candidate_reads_thesis\": \"the CANDIDATE should be judged with the THESIS's current conclusion in view, because the THESIS's answer bounds or drives the CANDIDATE's: a part read against its whole (one product line's sales against the company's total sales; one region's loan book against the bank's total loans), or a quantity read against another it depends on (a component supplier's revenue against its largest customer's capital spending; an airline's fuel bill against its fuel volume)\"\n    60\t \"thesis_reads_candidate\": \"the THESIS should be judged with the CANDIDATE's current conclusion in view, for the same reasons with the roles swapped\"\n    61\t \"neither\": \"neither answer bounds or drives the other: unrelated quantities (a retailer's gross margin and its store openings in another country), or the same quantity for the same period and scope; sharing a company, industry or topic is not enough\"\n    62\t\n    63\tSIGN, two builders with the same three classes; state = CANDIDATE (candidate_state), per pair:\n    64\t when the CANDIDATE reads the THESIS: \"If the THESIS's answer turned out higher, which way would that move the CANDIDATE's most likely answer? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text(T)\n    65\t when the THESIS reads the CANDIDATE: \"If the CANDIDATE's answer turned out higher, which way would that move the THESIS's most likely answer? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text(T)\n    66\t \"together\": \"a higher answer to the question read makes a higher answer to the question reading it more likely (a product line's sales and the company's total sales)\"\n    67\t \"opposite\": \"a higher answer to the question read makes a lower answer to the question reading it more likely (fuel prices and an airline's operating margin)\"\n    68\t \"no_clear_sign\": \"the question read only caps the other without moving its most likely answer (a ceiling far above any plausible outcome), or the supplied text does not show which way it moves it\"\n    69\t```\n    70\t\n    71\tSources: PRD 06 (\"B depending on A means B reads A's conclusion\"; a numeric thesis reading another numeric thesis), D51 (chosen in the\n    72\tmatching step), D537 and council R (a part reads its whole), judging-v7 lines 4 and 9 (\"a part cannot exceed its whole\"; \"consistent\n    73\twith the conclusions of the theses it depends on\"). Every class has an example from another industry (retail, banking, airlines,\n    74\tcomponents), all number questions of the kind D695 admits; none names a company. Same-quantity-same-period is excluded because such a pair is one question (D248); another period of the\n    75\tsame quantity may be linked. A link with no sign is not written: the existing label vocabulary cannot express it (council R round 2).\n    76\t\n    77\t**Decision rule (code):** Jev's returned `choice` decides, accepted only when its probability is at least 0.5 (`THRESHOLD`, as every Jev\n    78\tanswer in `jev_matching` is read). Stage 1 `neither` or below 0.5: no link. Stage 2 `no_clear_sign` or below 0.5: no link. Every\n    79\toutcome is in the selection record.\n    80\t\n    81\t## 3. What the reader is shown (judging-v8)\n    82\t\n    83\t```\n    84\t- v14 (open; first_is_bullish) How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-12\n    85\t    Comparison point stated by that judgement: <reference, or \"not stated\">\n    86\t    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): <implied_outcome, or \"not stated\">\n    87\t    Reasons (excerpt): <reasons, first 600 characters>\n    88\t```\n    89\tIndented lines start with four spaces and a word, never \"- v\" or \"[\", so neither `evidence_shown_in`, `themes_shown_in` nor a block\n    90\theader can read them; a value holding line breaks has each continuation line indented by eight spaces, so every physical line stays\n    91\tinside its block. Not judged yet: \"now not judged yet\" and nothing more. `store.current_state` also returns `reference` and\n    92\t`implied_outcome` (no v7 reader prints the whole dictionary). A change of the read question's comparison point alone, with its rung and\n    93\t`changed` unchanged, reaches the reader at the reader's next judgement, not in the same round (the round queues on `changed`, as for\n    94\tevery dependency today).\n    95\t\n    96\t## 4. The graph, the circle correction and the writer\n    97\t\n    98\t- **Graph check (one owner, `links.check_graph`, run at selection and again inside the write savepoint):** the reading relation =\n    99\t  every stored dependency row (all kinds) plus **every proposed link of the article**, the canonical candidates as nodes. Any circle\n   100\t  in that whole graph is found, including one through two openings and no stored path (C1 → T1 → C2 → T2 → C1).\n   101\t- **Waiting rows (admission):** under `jev-links` the link step refuses a store holding an unbound waiting row (a `dependencies` row\n   102\t  with a waited year and no target), failing the article at `matched` with that reason; so no waiting row can bind in the same write\n   103\t  and close a circle unseen. Product stores hold none (the three poc-v118 draws: 0 dependency rows); a test exercises the refusal.\n   104\t- **Correction (PRD 06: \"Refuse a cycle and ask the model to correct it; persistent cycles follow normal failure handling\"):** for each\n   105\t  proposed link on a circle, one correction request: the stage-1 question for that pair again, its instructions extended with \"Reading\n   106\t  this way would make <R> read itself through <path>; a question cannot read its own conclusion.\" and the offending direction removed\n   107\t  from the criteria. Each corrected pair's answer replaces its original; a new direction goes through stage 2; the whole set is\n   108\t  checked again. The rejected direction and its path are recorded. A circle that remains fails the article at `matched` (\"persistent\n   109\t  cycle\"), resumable, as PRD 06 says.\n   110\t- **Labels (code, §5)** are computed from the rungs as stored, inside the write, after C exists.\n   111\t- **Writer:** a link C reads T is written in step 2 with C's other dependencies; a link T reads C after C is created. Each row: the\n   112\t  article's seq, `direction` = the label, `kind = 'reads'`; T, when it is the reader, is added to the article's `changed` set, so the\n   113\t  day's round judges it after C when T is eligible (open, evidence in force, D59); a new C without evidence in force stays unjudged\n   114\t  and T reads it as \"not judged yet\". The plan is re-checked inside the write transaction (the graph, T still open); a mismatch raises\n   115\t  `WriteConflict` as today (the article fails, resumable).\n   116\t- **Store:** `dependencies.kind` (text). `ensure_writable_columns` adds it with default `''`; every existing row reads `''`.\n   117\t- **Filing:** `store.direct_parents` skips `kind = 'reads'` (D694 (a)); rows with `''` narrow exactly as today. `research_context`\n   118\t  reads dependency rows through an explicit column list (today `select *`), so its output keeps its shape.\n   119\t\n   120\t## 5. The label\n   121\t\n   122\t- **Typed direction** of a ladder (`links.typed_direction`): each rung is the interval [lo, hi) of its typed bounds; only the first\n   123\t  and the last rung may leave one outer end open (None); every inner rung has both bounds with lo < hi; an interval with lo ≥ hi is\n   124\t  invalid. The ladder runs −1 (values fall) when for every adjacent pair the next rung's hi is not above this rung's lo (touching\n   125\t  allowed), +1 when for every adjacent pair the next rung's lo is not below this rung's hi; anything else, an open inner end, or a\n   126\t  missing bound is None. Prose is not read (unlike `matching.ladder_direction`).\n   127\t- **The favourable end** is the end whose stored label is Strongly bullish (position 1, or position 5 for a successor stored\n   128\t  reversed). **Asset reader R reading T:** R's favourable end is its high end when that end is where R's values are high. T's end favourable to R: `together` → T's high end if R's favourable end is high, else\n   129\t  T's low end; `opposite` → the reverse. Label `first_is_bullish` when that end is T's first rung (T's high end is its first rung when\n   130\t  T's direction is −1), else `last_is_bullish`.\n   131\t- Worked case (old-2 07-10): R = v9 (direction −1, Strongly bullish first: favourable end high), T = v14 (−1), `together` → T's high\n   132\t  end = its first rung → `first_is_bullish`. Changing only the sign, only R's direction (its favourable end kept first), or only T's\n   133\t  direction each gives `last_is_bullish`; R stored reversed with its labels (favourable end last, direction +1) keeps the favourable\n   134\t  end high and gives `first_is_bullish`.\n   135\t- Eligibility (§1) already requires both directions decided, so a label is always defined for an asked pair.\n   136\t\n   137\t## 6. Table 1: state × event (C new in this article, T open and shown)\n   138\t\n   139\t| Event | Outcome |\n   140\t|---|---|\n   141\t| matching settles C as `new`/`succession`; the pair is eligible; READS and SIGN pass | link proposed; graph check; written in C's commit; reader judged in that day's round after the read question, if eligible (D59) |\n   142\t| READS `neither` / below 0.5; SIGN `no_clear_sign` / below 0.5 | no link; recorded |\n   143\t| C merges into an existing question, is skipped or not opened, or coalesces with another candidate | not asked, or asked once for the canonical candidate |\n   144\t| a pair not eligible (theme, event, two-rung, untyped or shuffled bounds, same article) | not asked (D695) |\n   145\t| a proposed link closes a circle (with stored links, or among the article's own proposals) | one correction request per link on it; a remaining circle fails the article at `matched`, resumable |\n   146\t| the store holds an unbound waiting row | the link step refuses: the article fails at `matched` with that reason |\n   147\t| `jev.ask` fails (transport, answer shape) | the article fails at `matched`, resumable; a resume re-asks what the archive lacks |\n   148\t| the plan no longer fits at write time (T closed in between, a circle) | `WriteConflict`; the article fails, resumable |\n   149\t| a crash after selection and before the write | resume re-runs matching and selection from the archive (no new send) and writes once |\n   150\t| a crash after the write | the link is in the article's commit; a resumed day's round rebuilds its queue (`queued_by_ledger`) |\n   151\t| T's conclusion changes in a round | its reader queued once, after it (`queued_by_change`) |\n   152\t| T's comparison point changes with `changed=true` | the reader is queued in the same round and sees it |\n   153\t| T's comparison point changes with `changed=false` | the reader sees it at its next judgement (§3) |\n   154\t| T closes | the reader keeps reading T's closing conclusion marked \"closed\" (PRD 06's numeric branch) |\n   155\t| the reader closes | not judged; the row stays as history |\n   156\t| a later article shows C and T again | not asked: neither is new (two open questions are a later version) |\n   157\t| an awaited (waiting) row in the store | this version writes none; the admission rule above refuses a store holding one |\n   158\t| a second process writing the same store | the July harness takes `live_lock.acquire` on each sequence's store for the life of the run (refused if held); the product's serial replay has no cross-process exclusion today and this version adds none: running two writers on one store is outside its operating contract, as for poc-v118 |\n   159\t| paid calls in flight when a run stops | an answered call is archived; an item without its commit is resumed and re-asks only what the archive lacks |\n   160\t| a version switch between completed days | allowed: the store's links and kinds are read the same by either version (§0); the July test switches from poc-v118 to poc-v119 at 07-10 |\n   161\t| a restart midway through a day under another configuration or with changed input | not supported and not detected by the serial path (the parallel day's manifest detects it); the harness never does it; the call records carry the checksum for a reader |\n   162\t| a v118 run on a v119 store | §0 |\n   163\t\n   164\t## 7. Table 2: value × reader\n   165\t\n   166\t| Value | Readers |\n   167\t|---|---|\n   168\t| `dependencies` row with `kind='reads'` | judging: `topological`, `upstream`, `build_prompt`, `check_answer`, `queued_by_change`, `queued_by_ledger`; `store.would_cycle`, `dependants_of`, `dependencies_of`; `links.check_graph`; the service (`dependencies`, `dependants`), `bundle`, `search` records, `research_context` (explicit columns), the idea route: all read \"R depends on T\". `store.direct_parents` (filing) skips it. |\n   169\t| `kind=''` | every reader as today |\n   170\t| the `link_selections` row | the July test's readers and its shape test; no product reader, not preflight, not the trace |\n   171\t| T added to `changed` | `round.changed_views_of_day` → `judge_day` |\n   172\t| `current_state.reference`, `.implied_outcome` | the judging-v8 block only |\n   173\t\n   174\t## 8. Table 3: new path × old checks\n   175\t\n   176\t| Check | Under poc-v119 |\n   177\t|---|---|\n   178\t| no-link requests byte-equal | proved at $0: poc-v119 over old-2's 07-01..07-09 with the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport equals the rebuilt v118 prefix (every other request from the archive) |\n   179\t| filing under seed-style rows | unchanged (`kind ''`); the existing test stays green |\n   180\t| filing with a `reads` row | no link removed: re-file old-2's stored readings after seq 148 with the link present (105 shared statements, `filing-exposure.md`) |\n   181\t| `cites_views` only names shown dependencies | unchanged |\n   182\t| dependencies judged first | unchanged |\n   183\t| `matching.check` refusals fail the article | selection runs after it and never adds to its refusals |\n   184\t| preflight and the trace (read `match_records` by `call_no`) | untouched: the selection is in `link_selections` |\n   185\t| D59, the theme block | unchanged |\n   186\t| frozen-piece pins | §0 |\n   187\t\n   188\t## 9. Table 4: prior decisions\n   189\t\n   190\tD51, D368 item 2 (the matching step chooses: a Jev question); D191 point 2 (an existing question gains a link when the read question\n   191\topens); D695 (number questions only, one new); D207, D265, D694 (a) (a link moves no statement); D260 (the reader sees the comparison\n   192\tpoint and the forecast); D248 (same quantity and period is one question); PRD 06 (cycles corrected, then normal failure); D354, D359\n   193\t(new versions); D542's five items: a circle through a waiting link cannot arise (no waiting link is written), closing as table 1,\n   194\ttheme twice and historical readers not reached (no theme link, no resolution row), `last_end` absent.\n   195\t\n   196\t## 10. Round-4 findings and where they are answered\n   197\t\n   198\tRound 5: 1 sign batching: §1 step 4, §2. 2 the whole graph and waits: §4. 3 archive: `TEST-PLAN.md`. 4 placement, interface, record:\n   199\t§1 steps 6–7. 5 reversed successors, event measures, intervals: §1 step 2, §5. 6 July dry run, extra links, budget: `TEST-PLAN.md`.\n   200\t7 restart and judging rows: §6. Renderer continuation lines: §3.\n   201\tRound 4: 1 final identity: §1 steps 1–2. 2 one graph, refusals recorded, PRD 06 correction: §1 step 6, §4. 3 lifecycle and theme boundary:\n   202\tD695, §6. 4 July harness: `TEST-PLAN.md` (archive, sequences, dry run, unexpected links, budget). 5 question texts: §2. 6 typed\n   203\tladders: §5. 7 failure and restart rows: §6. Compatibility (current_state, research_context, mixing, pins, entry points): §0, §3, §4.\n   204\t\n   205\t## 11. Tests (with the code; each names its row)\n   206\t\n   207\t1. `typed_direction` and the label: the worked case, its three mirrors, a reversed stored successor, a shuffled middle, touching and\n   208\t   overlapping bounds, an open inner end, prose-only bounds (None).\n   209\t2. Selection under `jev-links` with a fake Jev transport: eligibility (theme, two-rung, same-article and merge cases not asked);\n   210\t   stage 1 and 2 decisions; the canonical candidate asked once; under `jev` no question asked (mutant: asked).\n   211\t3. Graph and correction: a circle with a stored path corrected; the four-link circle through two openings found and corrected; a\n   212\t   persistent circle fails the article; a store with a waiting row refused; no circle written.\n   213\t4. Writer: T reads C written with `kind='reads'`, T in `changed`; WriteConflict when T closed.\n   214\t5. Filing: `direct_parents` skips `reads` (mutant: it narrows); seed-style rows narrow (existing test).\n   215\t6. judging-v8 block exact text, with a multi-line comparison point, forecast and reasons; v7 block byte-equal to today's; no-link\n   216\t   request byte-equal under v7 and v8; a comparison-point change with `changed=true` queues the reader, with `changed=false` does not.\n   217\t8. `link_selections` shape pinned; `writing.write`'s existing six-argument callers (`tests/test_identity_repair.py`) unchanged.\n   218\t7. Entry points: `config.load` accepts `jev-links`; `scripts/replay.py` and the parallel day treat it as Jev.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\nrg --files docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design | rg 'archive|r5|round6|prefix|filing'\nrg -n '\"'^## D69[4-9]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\nrg --files docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design | rg 'archive|r5|round6|prefix|filing'\nrg -n '\"'^## D69[4-9]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The July test: harness, archive, budget and reading rule (D694 (c); for council review before code)\n     2\t\n     3\t## Starting state ($0, done)\n     4\t`rebuild_control.py` → `rebuild-control.log`: old-2 replayed under poc-v118 from 07-01 to 07-09 with a transport that refuses every\n     5\tsend (`only_objects={'NVDA'}`, the comparison launcher's default): 160 items, 55 judgements, all from the archive; equal to old-2's\n     6\tfinished store up to seq 147 on views, keys, rungs, evidence, links, judgements (rung, reasons, cites, changed, reference, implied\n     7\toutcome, request sha), view switches, successions and dependencies. Each sequence starts from its own copy of this ledger.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Before any send ($0, to be built and run)\n    10\t1. **Prefix compatibility:** poc-v119 over 07-01..07-09 from empty, the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport, every\n    11\t   other request from the archive: the ledger equals the rebuilt prefix. This proves only that v119 with no link reproduces the\n    12\t   prefix; what a live v119 would have selected before 07-10 is not counted, and the linked arm starts from the v118 prefix by design\n    13\t   (the July test accepts the existing-reader / new-target case only, D694 (b)). The eligible pairs v119 would have asked before\n    14\t   07-10 are listed from the run's `link_selections` so the reader can see them.\n    15\t2. **The archive, proved:** each sequence's archive is a writable copy of old-2's archive (call ids kept) in which every stored judge\n    16\t   row for v9 or v14 (request user text beginning \"Thesis v9 (\" or \"Thesis v14 (\") is retired by the existing `Archive.retire`\n    17\t   (its request sha gains a suffix), so no exact lookup can return it. At $0 with a recording fake transport: an exact old v9 request\n    18\t   goes to the transport; an exact old request of another question is answered from the archive; an answer the check refuses is\n    19\t   retired and is not returned again.\n    20\t3. **Dry run:** the whole harness for 07-10..07-12 with a fixed fake transport for every call that would be bought: two control and\n    21\t   two linked dry sequences whose 07-10 answers for v9 and v14 differ (labelled \"DRY-A\", \"DRY-B\"). Every request that runs after the\n    22\t   first must carry its own sequence's last accepted answer. The control must judge v9 only on the days the stored run did (no v9\n    23\t   judgement on 07-11). The linked dry sequences must write \"v9 reads v14\" at seq 148 (fixed Jev answers) and show the judging-v8 block\n    24\t   in v9's requests; one with v14 `changed=true` on 07-11 must queue v9 that day, one with `changed=false` must not. Every other\n    25\t   request must be answered from the archive.\n    26\t4. **The rebuilt requests priced** at published rates (`model.PRICES`) to set the reservation; the reading rule frozen.\n    27\t\n    28\t## The sequences\n    29\tThree linked (poc-v119) and three control (poc-v118), each: its own copy of the prefix ledger; serial path (`replay.run`, no day\n    30\trunner); `only_objects={'NVDA'}`; 07-10 to 07-12.\n    31\t\n    32\t**Archive per sequence:** its own writable copy of old-2's archive with the v9 and v14 judge rows retired (step 2 above), so both\n    33\tquestions are judged fresh every day (council R round 3) and every other request replays by exact identity. The harness holds\n    34\t`live_lock.acquire` on each sequence's store for the run.\n    35\t\n    36\t**Transport:** the shared reservation ledger of the comparison runs (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py`\n    37\t`SharedLedger`, `BudgetTransport`, with `install_stop_gate`), one ceiling of **$0.15** for all six sequences, used as it behaves: a\n    38\tLuna call reserves its worst case per attempt and settles at its reported usage; a Jev call reserves its whole internal retry bundle\n    39\tand settles at up to the attempts times the reported usage, or at the reservation when usage is unavailable. After a sequence stops,\n    40\tthe shared ledger is read: a refused reservation makes the comparison **inconclusive**, even where `round.run` reports it as a matching\n    41\tor judging failure.\n    42\t\n    43\t**Expected new requests:** the v9 and v14 judge calls, the link questions of the item at seq 148 (linked arm), and a v9 judge call\n    44\ton any day it is queued by a changed v14. **Any other archive miss** (extraction, matching, another question's judgement) stops that\n    45\tsequence and is reported. Registered now for extra links the real selection may write besides \"v9 reads v14\" (for example with the\n    46\tstand-alone CPU question v8): the selection is kept and reported; a link whose reader is v9 or v14 changes a scored request and the\n    47\tsequence is scored as it ran, with the extra link named in the report; a link whose reader is any other question makes that\n    48\tquestion's request miss the archive, which stops the sequence as above, and the sequence counts as not comparable. A missing \"v9\n    49\treads v14\", or v14 reading v9, is a selection miss.\n    50\t\n    51\t## Reading rule (frozen before the send; council R round 2, `codex-r2.md` §7(b), with round 3)\n    52\t- **A. Comparable answers:** both 07-12 answers give a FY2027 forecast in USD for their own quantity (a range by its stated ends);\n    53\t  quarters recorded where both give comparable figures; a missing annual figure leaves reconciliation untested.\n    54\t- **B. Arithmetic and sources:** reported figures keep their amount and scope; the arithmetic follows from the stated inputs within\n    55\t  rounding; each assumption that materially sizes the result is disclosed and supported by the material available that day; a linked\n    56\t  forecast is treated as a forecast with assumptions.\n    57\t- **C. Room for the rest:** the high end of the Data Center forecast is at least $6B below the low end of the company forecast (the Q1\n    58\t  floor: $81.6B total minus $75.25B Data Center); each comparable quarter keeps the segment within the total.\n    59\t- **D. The link did the work (linked arm):** matching chose \"v9 reads v14\", the writer committed it at seq 148, and v9 used v14's\n    60\t  forecast in its calculation or as a stated bound; delivery and use of the Bloomberg-compiled $393B (e195) recorded separately; a\n    61\t  mention or citation alone earns no credit.\n    62\t- **Pass:** at least two of three linked sequences meet A–D; at most one control meets A–C; no first-attempt refusal added and no new\n    63\t  material grounding error on either question across 07-10..07-12 (relabelling a system forecast as a market estimate, or treating\n    64\t  $393B as a Data Center consensus, is one). **Inconclusive:** two or more controls reconcile, fewer than two comparable sequences in\n    65\t  either arm, or a ceiling stop. **Fail:** a new material error, an added refusal, fewer than two correct link selections, or any other\n    66\t  miss. Failures take precedence.\n    67\t- **Readers:** Claude's marks written first, then a fresh blind Codex reader on the six sequences under shuffled labels, the key outside\n    68\t  the repository; every sequence reported.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/filing-exposure.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r5.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r5.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round6-brief.md\n10439:## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n10454:## D695 · 2026-11-21 · Alex narrows the first linking version to number questions, one of them newly opened\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'retir|archive, proved|recording fake|v119|link_selections' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design --glob '*.py' --glob '*.log' --glob '*.md' --glob '\"'!codex-*.md'\"'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '49,65p;108,156p;175,206p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '27,61p;128,163p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '24,33p;54,70p;230,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'retir|archive, proved|recording fake|v119|link_selections' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design --glob '*.py' --glob '*.log' --glob '*.md' --glob '\"'!codex-*.md'\"'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '49,65p;108,156p;175,206p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '27,61p;128,163p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '24,33p;54,70p;230,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:10:1. **Prefix compatibility:** poc-v119 over 07-01..07-09 from empty, the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport, every\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:11:   other request from the archive: the ledger equals the rebuilt prefix. This proves only that v119 with no link reproduces the\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:12:   prefix; what a live v119 would have selected before 07-10 is not counted, and the linked arm starts from the v118 prefix by design\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:13:   (the July test accepts the existing-reader / new-target case only, D694 (b)). The eligible pairs v119 would have asked before\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:14:   07-10 are listed from the run's `link_selections` so the reader can see them.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:15:2. **The archive, proved:** each sequence's archive is a writable copy of old-2's archive (call ids kept) in which every stored judge\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:16:   row for v9 or v14 (request user text beginning \"Thesis v9 (\" or \"Thesis v14 (\") is retired by the existing `Archive.retire`\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:17:   (its request sha gains a suffix), so no exact lookup can return it. At $0 with a recording fake transport: an exact old v9 request\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:19:   retired and is not returned again.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:29:Three linked (poc-v119) and three control (poc-v118), each: its own copy of the prefix ledger; serial path (`replay.run`, no day\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:32:**Archive per sequence:** its own writable copy of old-2's archive with the v9 and v14 judge rows retired (step 2 above), so both\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:4:refused judge answer is retired in the copy only).\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:11:- `poc/config/poc-v119.json`: poc-v118 with `matching.engine` `jev-links` and `rejudging.prompt_version` `judging-v8`; nothing else.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:17:- **A store written by poc-v119 opened by poc-v118:** allowed; v118 writes no link, renders a stored link with today's v7 line, and\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:42:6. The selection is recorded in a **new table `link_selections`** (seq, input_id, config checksum, record_json: every pair shown with\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:47:   write does not commit is listed in the article's `written` notes and in `link_selections` (the write appends its outcome there).\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:160:| a version switch between completed days | allowed: the store's links and kinds are read the same by either version (§0); the July test switches from poc-v118 to poc-v119 at 07-10 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:162:| a v118 run on a v119 store | §0 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:170:| the `link_selections` row | the July test's readers and its shape test; no product reader, not preflight, not the trace |\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:176:| Check | Under poc-v119 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:178:| no-link requests byte-equal | proved at $0: poc-v119 over old-2's 07-01..07-09 with the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport equals the rebuilt v118 prefix (every other request from the archive) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:184:| preflight and the trace (read `match_records` by `call_no`) | untouched: the selection is in `link_selections` |\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:217:8. `link_selections` shape pinned; `writing.write`'s existing six-argument callers (`tests/test_identity_repair.py`) unchanged.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round6-brief.md:6:per sequence with the v9 and v14 judge rows retired through `Archive.retire`, proved at $0; the selection is a new table\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round6-brief.md:7:`link_selections`, not a `match_records` row; `proposed_links=None` keyword-only; reversed stored successors, event measures and\n    49\tdef resolve_waiting(conn, new_view_id, seq, changed):\n    50\t    \"\"\"A new view on a chain satisfies dependencies waiting for its year on that chain.\"\"\"\n    51\t    v = store.view(conn, new_view_id)\n    52\t    chain = {new_view_id}\n    53\t    frontier = [new_view_id]\n    54\t    while frontier:\n    55\t        current = frontier.pop()\n    56\t        for row in conn.execute('select succeeds from successions where view_id=?', (current,)):\n    57\t            if row['succeeds'] not in chain:\n    58\t                chain.add(row['succeeds'])\n    59\t                frontier.append(row['succeeds'])\n    60\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where wait_year=? and wait_chain_view_id is not null', (v['year'],)):\n    61\t        if dep['wait_chain_view_id'] in chain:\n    62\t            already = conn.execute('select 1 from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=?', (dep['dependency_id'],)).fetchone()\n    63\t            if not already and not store.would_cycle(conn, dep['view_id'], new_view_id):\n    64\t                store.insert(conn, 'dependency_resolutions', dependency_id=dep['dependency_id'], resolved_to=new_view_id, reason='created', seq=seq)\n    65\t                changed.add(dep['view_id'])\n   108\tclass WriteConflict(ValueError):\n   109\t    \"\"\"The checked plan no longer fits the writable ledger; no partial write is retained.\"\"\"\n   110\t\n   111\t\n   112\tdef write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass):\n   113\t    \"\"\"Write atomically within the caller's transaction; the caller commits the completion marker with it.\"\"\"\n   114\t    if not conn.in_transaction:\n   115\t        conn.execute('begin immediate')\n   116\t    conn.execute('savepoint view_write')\n   117\t    try:\n   118\t        store.ensure_writable_columns(conn)\n   119\t        result = _write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   120\t    except Exception:\n   121\t        conn.execute('rollback to view_write')\n   122\t        conn.execute('release view_write')\n   123\t        raise\n   124\t    conn.execute('release view_write')\n   125\t    return result\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\tdef _write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass):\n   129\t    \"\"\"second_pass: {(handover evidence id, view_id): (outcome, target_evidence_id, said_day)} for candidate-linked\n   130\t    evidence compared after the candidates' destinations were known (new views' evidence is simply new).\"\"\"\n   131\t    changed, notes, new_views, evidence_ids = set(), [], {}, {}\n   132\t    candidate_ids = {c['id'] for c in handover.candidates}\n   133\t    aliases, problems = identity.batch_plan(handover.candidates, checked.outcomes)\n   134\t    if problems:\n   135\t        raise WriteConflict('; '.join(problems))\n   136\t    created = {}\n   137\t    # 1. new views, themes first\n   138\t    order = sorted(handover.candidates, key=lambda c: 0 if c['kind'] == 'theme' else 1)\n   139\t    for c in order:\n   140\t        outcome, target, deps = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   141\t        if outcome not in ('new', 'succession'):\n   142\t            continue\n   143\t        canonical = aliases[c['id']]\n   144\t        if canonical in created:\n   145\t            new_views[c['id']] = created[canonical]\n   146\t            continue\n   147\t        if store.exact_key_views(conn, c):\n   148\t            raise WriteConflict(f'candidate {c[\"id\"]}: existing exact identity requires matching')\n   149\t        object_id = universe.resolve(c['object'])\n   150\t        if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n   151\t            c = oriented_like(c, store.rungs_of(conn, target), notes)\n   152\t        view_id = _create_view(conn, c, object_id, universe.kind(object_id), seq, item, universe)\n   153\t        new_views[c['id']] = view_id\n   154\t        created[canonical] = view_id\n   155\t        if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n   156\t            store.insert(conn, 'successions', view_id=view_id, succeeds=target, seq=seq)\n   175\t    # 2. dependencies of the new views (candidate ids resolve to the views just created)\n   176\t    dependencies_written = set()\n   177\t    for c in order:\n   178\t        outcome, target, deps = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   179\t        if c['id'] not in new_views:\n   180\t            continue\n   181\t        view_id = new_views[c['id']]\n   182\t        for dep in deps:\n   183\t            depends_on = dep['view_id']\n   184\t            if depends_on in new_views:\n   185\t                depends_on = new_views[depends_on]\n   186\t            elif depends_on in candidate_ids:\n   187\t                notes.append(f'dependency {view_id} -> candidate {depends_on} dropped: that candidate was not opened')\n   188\t                continue\n   189\t            if depends_on and store.would_cycle(conn, view_id, depends_on):\n   190\t                notes.append(f'dependency {view_id} -> {depends_on} dropped: cycle')\n   191\t                continue\n   192\t            chain = dep['wait_chain_view_id']\n   193\t            if chain in new_views:\n   194\t                chain = new_views[chain]\n   195\t            wait_year = dep['wait_year']\n   196\t            if wait_year and chain and hasattr(universe, 'canonical_year'):          # the chain's object decides the spelling (FY2027 or 2026)\n   197\t                chain_view = store.view(conn, chain)\n   198\t                wait_year = universe.canonical_year(chain_view['object_id'] if chain_view else object_id_of(universe, c), wait_year)\n   199\t            edge = (view_id, depends_on, chain, wait_year, dep['direction'])\n   200\t            if edge in dependencies_written:\n   201\t                continue\n   202\t            dependencies_written.add(edge)\n   203\t            store.insert(conn, 'dependencies', view_id=view_id, depends_on=depends_on, wait_chain_view_id=chain, wait_year=wait_year,\n   204\t                         direction=dep['direction'], seq=seq)\n   205\t        resolve_waiting(conn, view_id, seq, changed)\n   206\t    # 3. where each piece of evidence goes\n    27\tdef _fail(conn, item, seq, result, step, kind, detail, pool_key):\n    28\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, step, 'failed', detail[:300])\n    29\t    store.pool(conn, kind, pool_key, {'input_id': item['input_id'], 'error': detail[:300]}, seq)\n    30\t    result.failed = detail[:200]\n    31\t    conn.commit()\n    32\t    return result\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, candidates, evidence, lists, shown, *, extra_views=(), call_offset=0, transport=None, workers=1):\n    36\t    \"\"\"One matching call with one retry on a refused check. Returns Checked, or None after marking the failure.\"\"\"\n    37\t    note = ''\n    38\t    checked = None\n    39\t    engine = jev_matching if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else matching      # Jev answers once; a retry would be the same answer\n    40\t    for attempt in range(1 if engine is jev_matching else 2):\n    41\t        try:\n    42\t            options = {'workers': workers, 'llm_transport': transport} if engine is jev_matching else {}     # the collision judge sends with the caller's transport too\n    43\t            answer = engine.decide(archive, cfg, conn, item, candidates, evidence, lists, shown, extra_views=extra_views, retry_note=note, transport=transport, **options)\n    44\t        except Exception as error:\n    45\t            _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_failed', 'matching: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n    46\t            return None\n    47\t        result.cost += answer.cost_usd\n    48\t        result.cached_calls += int(answer.cached)\n    49\t        checked = matching.check(conn, universe, answer.data, candidates, evidence, lists, shown)\n    50\t        shown_record = {'candidates': lists.candidate_lists, 'evidence': {f'{k[0]}|{k[1]}': v for k, v in lists.evidence_lists.items()}}\n    51\t        if getattr(answer, 'request_records', None):\n    52\t            shown_record['requests'] = answer.request_records\n    53\t        store.insert(conn, 'match_records', seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], call_no=call_offset + attempt + 1,\n    54\t                     shown_json=json.dumps(shown_record),\n    55\t                     request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, call_id=answer.call_id, decisions_json=json.dumps(answer.data, ensure_ascii=False),\n    56\t                     checks_json=json.dumps({'refusals': checked.refusals, 'not_opened': checked.not_opened, 'notes': checked.notes}, ensure_ascii=False), written_json=None)\n    57\t        if not checked.refusals:\n    58\t            return checked\n    59\t        note = '；'.join(checked.refusals)\n    60\t    _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_refused_twice', 'matching refused twice: ' + note, item['category'])\n    61\t    return None\n   128\t    # first matching call: the candidates and the evidence linked straight to existing views\n   129\t    lists = matching.build_lists(conn, handover, shown, cfg.search_top_n)\n   130\t    checked = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, handover.candidates, handover.evidence, lists, shown, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   131\t    if checked is None:\n   132\t        return result\n   133\t    # second call: evidence linked to candidates that attached to an existing view, compared under that view\n   134\t    second_pass = {}\n   135\t    pending = []\n   136\t    for e in handover.evidence:\n   137\t        for link in e['links']:\n   138\t            outcome = checked.outcomes.get(link)\n   139\t            if outcome and outcome[0] == 'merge':\n   140\t                pending.append((e, outcome[1]))\n   141\t    if pending:\n   142\t        lists2 = matching.Lists({}, {(e['id'], view_id): matching.rank_evidence(conn, view_id, e['one_line'], cfg.search_top_n) for e, view_id in pending})\n   143\t        evidence2, seen = [], set()\n   144\t        for e, view_id in pending:\n   145\t            if e['id'] not in seen:\n   146\t                evidence2.append(dict(e, links=[v for x, v in pending if x['id'] == e['id']]))\n   147\t                seen.add(e['id'])\n   148\t        checked2 = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, [], evidence2, lists2, [], extra_views=sorted({v for _, v in pending}),\n   149\t                          call_offset=2, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   150\t        if checked2 is None:\n   151\t            return result\n   152\t        second_pass = checked2.evidence\n   153\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\n   154\t    # write, and record what changed in the same commit (a resume at 'judged' reads it)\n   155\t    try:\n   156\t        written = writing.write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   157\t    except Exception as error:\n   158\t        return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'written', 'writing_failed', 'writing: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   159\t    result.new_views = len(set(written.new_views.values()))\n   160\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'written', 'ok', json.dumps({'changed': sorted(written.changed_views), 'new': written.new_views, 'notes': written.notes[:20]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   161\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', '')\n   162\t    conn.commit()\n   163\t    return result\n    24\t    'same_claims': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, seq integer',                    # D204: the matcher read the new piece as the same claim as the old; both stored, both in force\n    25\t    'dependencies': 'dependency_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, depends_on text, wait_chain_view_id text, wait_year text, direction text, seq integer',\n    26\t    'dependency_resolutions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, dependency_id integer, resolved_to text, reason text, seq integer',\n    27\t    'successions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, succeeds text, seq integer',\n    28\t    'handovers': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, seq integer, handover_json text',\n    29\t    'match_records': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, seq integer, input_id text, call_no integer, shown_json text, request_sha256 text, call_id integer, decisions_json text, checks_json text, written_json text',\n    30\t    'processing_steps': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, sequence_no integer, step text, result text, reason text, publication_day text, at text',\n    31\t    'review_pool_entries': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, kind text, key text, example_json text, seq integer',\n    32\t    'late_statements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, evidence_quote text, reason text, seq integer',\n    33\t    'days_completed': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, day text, seq integer, at text',\n    54\t\n    55\tdef open_db(path):\n    56\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    57\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\n    58\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    59\t    for name, columns in TABLES.items():\n    60\t        conn.execute(f'create table if not exists {name} ({columns})')\n    61\t        conn.execute(f\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_update before update on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\")\n    62\t        conn.execute(f\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_delete before delete on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\")\n    63\t    for statement in INDEXES:\n    64\t        conn.execute(statement)\n    65\t    ensure_writable_columns(conn)\n    66\t    conn.execute(\"create virtual table if not exists views_fts using fts5(view_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\")\n    67\t    conn.execute(\"create virtual table if not exists groups_fts using fts5(group_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\")\n    68\t    conn.execute('create index if not exists members_view on thesis_group_members(view_id)')\n    69\t    conn.commit()\n    70\t    return conn\n   230\tdef current_state(conn, view_id):\n   231\t    row = conn.execute('select judgement_id, rung, reasons, changed, seq, publication_day from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n   232\t    return dict(row) if row else None\n   233\t\n   234\t\n   235\tdef dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\n   236\t    \"\"\"Each dependency with its current target: the resolved view, or the waiting chain and year.\"\"\"\n   237\t    out = []\n   238\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\n   239\t        dep = dict(dep)\n   240\t        resolution = conn.execute('select resolved_to, reason from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (dep['dependency_id'],)).fetchone()\n   241\t        if resolution:\n   242\t            dep['resolved_to'], dep['resolution'] = resolution['resolved_to'], resolution['reason']\n   243\t        else:\n   244\t            dep['resolved_to'], dep['resolution'] = dep['depends_on'], ('direct' if dep['depends_on'] else 'waiting')\n   245\t        out.append(dep)\n   246\t    return out\n   247\t\n   248\t\n   249\tdef direct_parents(conn, view_id, seq=None):\n   250\t    \"\"\"The views this view depends on directly (a driver's root, D208; the seeds' depends_on), written at or before `seq` when given.\n   251\t    The filing reads it to keep a statement under the narrower of two linked questions (D207's narrowest rule, extraction.file_reading).\"\"\"\n   252\t    rows = conn.execute(\"select depends_on from dependencies where view_id=? and depends_on != '' and (? is null or seq <= ?) order by dependency_id\", (view_id, seq, seq))\n   253\t    return list(dict.fromkeys(r[0] for r in rows))\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef dependants_of(conn, view_id):\n   257\t    direct = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,))]\n   258\t    resolved = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute(\n   259\t        'select d.view_id from dependency_resolutions r join dependencies d on d.dependency_id=r.dependency_id where r.resolved_to=?', (view_id,))]\n   260\t    return sorted(set(direct + resolved))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,131p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/dispatch.py | sed -n '20,55p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/live_lock.py | sed -n '36,74p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/parallel_day.py | sed -n '68,90p;131,153p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '78,112p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '69,105p;245,261p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,131p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/dispatch.py | sed -n '20,55p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/live_lock.py | sed -n '36,74p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/parallel_day.py | sed -n '68,90p;131,153p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '78,112p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '69,105p;245,261p'\"","aggregated_output":"    51\tdef run(*, testdb_path, views_path, archive, cfg, universe, from_day, until_day, day0=None, spend_cap_usd=None,\n    52\t        transport=None, log=print, only_objects=None, max_items_per_day=None, day_runner=None):\n    53\t    items_db = testdb.open_db(testdb_path)\n    54\t    conn = store.open_db(views_path)\n    55\t    refuse_unfinished_parallel(conn)\n    56\t    last_done = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    57\t    start = from_day\n    58\t    if last_done and from_day <= last_done:\n    59\t        next_day = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(last_done) + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat()\n    60\t        if next_day > until_day:\n    61\t            raise BackdatingError(f'views database already completed {last_done}; nothing to run before it')\n    62\t        log(f'resuming after the last completed day {last_done}')\n    63\t        start = next_day\n    64\t    last_written = conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0').fetchone()[0]\n    65\t    if last_written and start < last_written:\n    66\t        raise BackdatingError(f'views database already holds rounds of {last_written}; a replay cannot start before it (D31)')\n    67\t    totals = {'items': 0, 'extracted': 0, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 0, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0,\n    68\t              'evidence': 0, 'new_views': 0, 'judged': 0, 'changed': 0, 'closed': 0}\n    69\t    calls_before, cost_before, *_ = archive.totals()\n    70\t    for day in calendar_days(start, until_day):\n    71\t        day_stats = {k: 0 for k in totals}\n    72\t        day_cost_before = archive.totals()[1]\n    73\t        processed = 0\n    74\t        to_run = []\n    75\t        for item in testdb.feed(items_db, day, day):\n    76\t            if item['publication_day'] > day:\n    77\t                raise LookAheadError(f'{item[\"input_id\"]} is dated {item[\"publication_day\"]}, after replay day {day}')\n    78\t            if only_objects and not any(o['value'] in only_objects for o in item['object_identifiers']):\n    79\t                continue\n    80\t            if max_items_per_day and processed >= max_items_per_day:\n    81\t                break\n    82\t            day_stats['items'] += 1\n    83\t            route = dispatch.route(conn, item, universe)\n    84\t            if route.kind != 'extract':\n    85\t                day_stats[route.kind] += 1\n    86\t                if route.kind == 'skipped':\n    87\t                    processed += 1      # written by an earlier run of this day: a restart keeps the day's item limit\n    88\t                if route.kind == 'merged':\n    89\t                    dispatch.mark(conn, item, 0, 'merged', 'ok', route.reason)\n    90\t                    conn.commit()\n    91\t                continue\n    92\t            processed += 1\n    93\t            to_run.append((item, route))\n    94\t        results = (day_runner(conn, archive, cfg, universe, to_run, day=day, transport=transport, log=log) if day_runner else\n    95\t                   (round_module.run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, route.sequence_no, resume_from=route.resume_from, transport=transport, log=log)\n    96\t                    for item, route in to_run))\n    97\t        finished = 0\n    98\t        try:\n    99\t            for index, result in enumerate(results):\n   100\t                if index >= len(to_run) or result.input_id != to_run[index][0]['input_id']:\n   101\t                    raise RuntimeError('day runner returned results out of input order')\n   102\t                finished += 1\n   103\t                day_stats['extracted'] += 1\n   104\t                day_stats['evidence'] += result.evidence\n   105\t                day_stats['new_views'] += result.new_views\n   106\t                day_stats['judged'] += result.judged\n   107\t                day_stats['changed'] += result.changed\n   108\t                if result.failed:\n   109\t                    day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   110\t                    log(f'  ! {result.input_id[:60]}: {result.failed}')\n   111\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'item failed; day {day} remains resumable: {result.failed}')\n   112\t                if spend_cap_usd is not None and archive.totals()[1] - cost_before > spend_cap_usd:\n   113\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'spend cap {spend_cap_usd} reached on {day}')\n   114\t        finally:\n   115\t            if hasattr(results, 'close'):\n   116\t                results.close()\n   117\t        if finished != len(to_run):\n   118\t            raise RuntimeError('day runner did not complete every routed item')\n   119\t        seq = store.next_sequence(conn) - 1\n   120\t        judged = round_module.judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, transport=transport, log=log)\n   121\t        day_stats['judged'] += judged.judged\n   122\t        day_stats['changed'] += judged.changed\n   123\t        if judged.failed:\n   124\t            day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   125\t            log(f'  ! day judging: {judged.failed}')\n   126\t            raise RuntimeError(f'judging failed; day {day} remains resumable: {judged.failed}')\n   127\t        closed = pull.end_of_day(conn, day, seq)\n   128\t        day_stats['closed'] = len(closed)\n   129\t        # The day ends at the last sequence it wrote, a closing's own sequence on a day without items included, so the next day starts after it.\n   130\t        store.complete_day(conn, day, store.next_sequence(conn) - 1, time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   131\t        conn.commit()\n    20\tSTEPS = ('dispatched', 'extracted', 'matched', 'written', 'judged', 'handed_over')\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\tdef route(conn, item, universe):\n    24\t    missing = [field for field in REQUIRED if not item.get(field)]\n    25\t    if missing:\n    26\t        store.pool(conn, 'incomplete_item', ','.join(missing), {'input_id': item.get('input_id'), 'missing': missing}, 0)\n    27\t        return Route('returned', reason=f'missing {missing}')\n    28\t    input_id = item['input_id']\n    29\t    if store.is_processed(conn, input_id):\n    30\t        return Route('skipped', reason='already processed')\n    31\t    last = store.last_step(conn, input_id)\n    32\t    if last and last['step'] in STEPS and last['sequence_no']:\n    33\t        # unfinished work keeps its sequence number: after an ok step it continues at the next step, after a\n    34\t        # failed step it retries that step (06-views: 失败从失败的那一步重试)\n    35\t        position = STEPS.index(last['step'])\n    36\t        resume_from = STEPS[position + 1] if last['result'] == 'ok' else last['step']\n    37\t        return Route('extract', sequence_no=last['sequence_no'], resume_from=resume_from, reason='resuming')\n    38\t    if item.get('copy_of'):\n    39\t        return Route('merged', reason=f'copy of {item[\"copy_of\"]}')\n    40\t    if item.get('supersedes'):\n    41\t        store.pool(conn, 'correction_not_supported', item['supersedes'], {'input_id': input_id}, 0)\n    42\t        return Route('not_processed', reason='correction (supersedes) not supported in the POC')\n    43\t    category = item['category']\n    44\t    objects = [o['value'] for o in item.get('object_identifiers') or [] if universe.has(o['value'])]\n    45\t    if not objects:\n    46\t        return Route('not_processed', reason='no object on the research list')\n    47\t    if not any(universe.watches(o, category) for o in objects):\n    48\t        return Route('not_processed', reason=f'category {category} not watched for {objects}')\n    49\t    # the sequence number is taken in arrival order and written at once, so two items routed before either is\n    50\t    # processed (a whole day is routed first, then run) never share a number\n    51\t    sequence_no = store.next_sequence(conn)\n    52\t    store.mark_step(conn, input_id, sequence_no, 'dispatched', 'ok', '', item.get('publication_day'), time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n    53\t    conn.commit()\n    54\t    return Route('extract', sequence_no=sequence_no, reason='')\n    55\t\n    36\t        raise LockRefused(f'the lock folder {LOCK_FOLDER} cannot be written')\n    37\t    return LOCK_FOLDER\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\tdef own_path(store_path):\n    41\t    \"\"\"(the store's real path, (device, inode)); a store with another hard link is refused.\"\"\"\n    42\t    real = os.path.realpath(store_path)\n    43\t    status = os.stat(real)\n    44\t    if status.st_nlink > 1:\n    45\t        raise LockRefused(f'{real} has {status.st_nlink} hard links: a store is opened only by its own path')\n    46\t    return real, (status.st_dev, status.st_ino)\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tclass Held:\n    50\t    \"\"\"A held lock: the store's real path and identity, the lock file's path, descriptor and inode.\"\"\"\n    51\t\n    52\t    def __init__(self, real_path, identity, lock_path, descriptor):\n    53\t        self.real_path, self.identity, self.lock_path, self.descriptor = real_path, identity, lock_path, descriptor\n    54\t        self.lock_inode = os.fstat(descriptor).st_ino\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef acquire(store_path):\n    58\t    \"\"\"The store's lock, without waiting: refused when another process holds it.\"\"\"\n    59\t    real, identity = own_path(store_path)\n    60\t    lock_path = os.path.join(lock_folder(), f'{identity[0]}-{identity[1]}.writer.lock')\n    61\t    descriptor = os.open(lock_path, os.O_CREAT | os.O_RDWR, 0o600)\n    62\t    try:\n    63\t        fcntl.flock(descriptor, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n    64\t    except BlockingIOError:\n    65\t        os.close(descriptor)\n    66\t        raise LockRefused(f'{real} is being written (its lock is held): read a snapshot of it instead (scripts/snapshot_store.py)') from None\n    67\t    held = Held(real, identity, lock_path, descriptor)\n    68\t    try:\n    69\t        verify(held)\n    70\t    except BaseException:\n    71\t        release(held)\n    72\t        raise\n    73\t    return held\n    74\t\n    68\t    def _manifest(self, conn, cfg, universe, items, day):\n    69\t        self.manifest_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    70\t        path = self.manifest_dir / f'day-{day}.json'\n    71\t        metadata = {'day': day, 'environment': environment_key(cfg, universe), 'runtime': runtime_key(),\n    72\t                    'source': digest(self.source_path), 'extraction_workers': self.extraction_workers,\n    73\t                    'jev_workers': self.jev_workers}\n    74\t        entries = [{'input_id': item['input_id'], 'seq': route.sequence_no, 'hash': item_key(item)} for item, route in items]\n    75\t        started = conn.execute(\"select 1 from processing_steps where publication_day=? and step in ('extracted','written','handed_over') limit 1\", (day,)).fetchone()\n    76\t        if not started:\n    77\t            # Nothing of this day is written in this ledger: a manifest left by another run or ledger guards nothing here.\n    78\t            path.write_text(json.dumps(dict(metadata, inputs=entries), sort_keys=True), encoding='utf-8')\n    79\t        elif not path.exists():\n    80\t            raise ValueError('cannot adopt a partially processed day without its parallel-day manifest; finish it with --workers 1')\n    81\t        try:\n    82\t            saved = json.loads(path.read_text())\n    83\t        except (OSError, ValueError) as error:\n    84\t            raise ValueError('unreadable parallel-day manifest; refusing to guess its inputs') from error\n    85\t        if {k: saved.get(k) for k in metadata} != metadata:\n    86\t            raise ValueError('parallel-day manifest source, configuration or runtime changed')\n    87\t        remaining = [entry for entry in saved['inputs'] if not store.is_processed(conn, entry['input_id'])]\n    88\t        if remaining != entries:\n    89\t            raise ValueError('parallel-day manifest input order or content changed')\n    90\t        return metadata\n   131\t        def accepted_extraction(current_archive, current_cfg, item, text, shown, current_universe, *, transport=None):\n   132\t            prior_key, source_key, future, _ = pending[item['input_id']]\n   133\t            def validate_inputs():\n   134\t                if (environment_key(current_cfg, current_universe) != metadata['environment']\n   135\t                        or environment_key(cfg, universe) != metadata['environment'] or runtime_key() != metadata['runtime']):\n   136\t                    raise ValueError('configuration, universe or runtime changed during the day')\n   137\t                if item_key(item) != source_key or text != item['text']:\n   138\t                    raise ValueError('source changed after preparation')\n   139\t            validate_inputs()\n   140\t            current_key = extraction_key(current_cfg, item, text, shown, current_universe)\n   141\t            if current_key == prior_key:\n   142\t                reading = future.result()\n   143\t                validate_inputs()\n   144\t                if reading.answer.request_sha256 != current_key:\n   145\t                    raise ValueError('prepared extraction does not match its validated request')\n   146\t                self._event(item['input_id'], 'reused', request=current_key)\n   147\t                return extraction.file_reading(reading, item, shown)   # filed under the questions open now\n   148\t            future.cancel()\n   149\t            self._event(item['input_id'], 'stale', before=prior_key, request=current_key)\n   150\t            reading = extraction.read_item(current_archive, current_cfg, item, text, shown, current_universe, transport=transport)\n   151\t            validate_inputs()\n   152\t            self._event(item['input_id'], 'reextracted', request=current_key)\n   153\t            return extraction.file_reading(reading, item, shown)\n    78\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: choice is not the most probable option')\n    79\t    return problems\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\tdef request_for(setting, state, questions):\n    83\t    \"\"\"The complete Jev request used both for dispatch and in-flight identity.\"\"\"\n    84\t    return {'model': setting.model, 'state': state, 'questions': questions}\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef ask(archive, cfg, setting, state, questions, purpose, *, transport=None):\n    88\t    \"\"\"One Jev request, archived; returns model.Answer whose data is the `answers` map.\"\"\"\n    89\t    request = request_for(setting, state, questions)\n    90\t    request_json, sha = model.request_identity(request)\n    91\t    prompt_chars = len(request_json)\n    92\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n    93\t    if hit:\n    94\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n    95\t        return model.Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n    96\t    started = time.time()\n    97\t    response = (transport or globals()['transport'])(request)\n    98\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 2)\n    99\t    answers = response.get('answers') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   100\t    problems = validate(answers, questions)\n   101\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {} if isinstance(response, dict) else {}\n   102\t    input_tokens, output_tokens = int(usage.get('input_tokens') or 0), int(usage.get('output_tokens') or 0)\n   103\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   104\t    cost = round(input_tokens / 1e6 * price_in, 6)\n   105\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   106\t                             request_sha256=sha if not problems else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   107\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response, ensure_ascii=False)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(answers, ensure_ascii=False) if answers is not None else None,\n   108\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   109\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   110\t    if problems:\n   111\t        raise model.SchemaError('; '.join(problems[:5]))\n   112\t    return model.Answer(answers, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n    69\tclass Archive:\n    70\t    \"\"\"Shared by the extraction worker threads: one connection, every access under a lock.\"\"\"\n    71\t\n    72\t    def __init__(self, path):\n    73\t        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    74\t        self.conn = sqlite3.connect(path, check_same_thread=False)\n    75\t        self.conn.executescript(SCHEMA_SQL)\n    76\t        import threading\n    77\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n    78\t\n    79\t    def lookup(self, sha):\n    80\t        with self.lock:\n    81\t            return self.conn.execute('select call_id, answer_json, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (sha,)).fetchone()\n    82\t\n    83\t    def record(self, **fields):\n    84\t        \"\"\"One row per distinct request; a second identical request recorded at the same moment (two threads, or a\n    85\t        failed answer repeated within the same second) keeps the first row's id instead of failing.\"\"\"\n    86\t        columns = list(fields)\n    87\t        with self.lock:\n    88\t            cursor = self.conn.execute(f'insert or ignore into model_calls ({\",\".join(columns)}) values ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(columns))})',\n    89\t                                       [fields[c] for c in columns])\n    90\t            self.conn.commit()\n    91\t            if cursor.rowcount == 0:\n    92\t                return self.conn.execute('select call_id from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (fields['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()[0]\n    93\t            return cursor.lastrowid\n    94\t\n    95\t    def retire(self, call_id):\n    96\t        \"\"\"A code check refused this answer: the row stays for the record, but no later identical request is answered with it\n    97\t        (the same shape as a schema-refused or malformed row, whose hash carries a suffix).\"\"\"\n    98\t        with self.lock:\n    99\t            self.conn.execute(\"update model_calls set request_sha256 = request_sha256 || ':refused:' || ? where call_id=? and request_sha256 not like '%:refused:%'\",\n   100\t                              (uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], call_id))\n   101\t            self.conn.commit()\n   102\t\n   103\t    def totals(self):\n   104\t        with self.lock:\n   105\t            return self.conn.execute('select count(*), coalesce(sum(cost_usd),0), coalesce(sum(input_tokens),0), coalesce(sum(output_tokens),0) from model_calls').fetchone()\n   245\tdef request_identity(request):\n   246\t    \"\"\"The exact serialized request and its archive key, shared by callers and validation.\"\"\"\n   247\t    encoded = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n   248\t    return encoded, hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\tdef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   252\t    provider = cfg.provider\n   253\t    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n   254\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   255\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   256\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   257\t    if hit:\n   258\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   259\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   260\t    started = time.time()\n   261\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c '\nimport threading, sqlite3, json, re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom hivemind import model\nf=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite\\\").resolve()\na=object.__new__(model.Archive)\na.conn=sqlite3.connect(\\\":memory:\\\")\na.conn.executescript(model.SCHEMA_SQL)\na.lock=threading.Lock()\nwith sqlite3.connect(f.as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True) as c:\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n picked={}\n for row in c.execute(\\\"select * from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\'' and instr(request_sha256, '\\\\'':'\\\\'')=0 order by call_id\\\"):\n  request=json.loads(row[\\\"request_json\\\"])\n  m=re.match(r\\\"Thesis (v\\\\d+) \\\\(\\\",request[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"])\n  if m and m[1] in (\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v8\\\") and m[1] not in picked:\n   picked[m[1]]=dict(row)\n  if len(picked)==3:break\nfor row in picked.values():\n assert a.record(**row)==row[\\\"call_id\\\"]\nfor name in (\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\"):\n r=picked[name]\n assert a.lookup(r[\\\"request_sha256\\\"])[0]==r[\\\"call_id\\\"]\n a.retire(r[\\\"call_id\\\"])\n assert a.lookup(r[\\\"request_sha256\\\"]) is None\n v=a.conn.execute(\\\"select request_sha256 from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(r[\\\"call_id\\\"],)).fetchone()[0]\n assert v.startswith(r[\\\"request_sha256\\\"]+\\\":refused:\\\")\nassert a.lookup(picked[\\\"v8\\\"][\\\"request_sha256\\\"])[0]==picked[\\\"v8\\\"][\\\"call_id\\\"]\nprint(\\\"Confirmed on 3 real archived requests in memory: v9/v14 keys masked; unrelated v8 still hits; archived IDs kept.\\\")\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c '\nimport threading, sqlite3, json, re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom hivemind import model\nf=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite\\\").resolve()\na=object.__new__(model.Archive)\na.conn=sqlite3.connect(\\\":memory:\\\")\na.conn.executescript(model.SCHEMA_SQL)\na.lock=threading.Lock()\nwith sqlite3.connect(f.as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True) as c:\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n picked={}\n for row in c.execute(\\\"select * from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\'' and instr(request_sha256, '\\\\'':'\\\\'')=0 order by call_id\\\"):\n  request=json.loads(row[\\\"request_json\\\"])\n  m=re.match(r\\\"Thesis (v\\\\d+) \\\\(\\\",request[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"])\n  if m and m[1] in (\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v8\\\") and m[1] not in picked:\n   picked[m[1]]=dict(row)\n  if len(picked)==3:break\nfor row in picked.values():\n assert a.record(**row)==row[\\\"call_id\\\"]\nfor name in (\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\"):\n r=picked[name]\n assert a.lookup(r[\\\"request_sha256\\\"])[0]==r[\\\"call_id\\\"]\n a.retire(r[\\\"call_id\\\"])\n assert a.lookup(r[\\\"request_sha256\\\"]) is None\n v=a.conn.execute(\\\"select request_sha256 from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(r[\\\"call_id\\\"],)).fetchone()[0]\n assert v.startswith(r[\\\"request_sha256\\\"]+\\\":refused:\\\")\nassert a.lookup(picked[\\\"v8\\\"][\\\"request_sha256\\\"])[0]==picked[\\\"v8\\\"][\\\"call_id\\\"]\nprint(\\\"Confirmed on 3 real archived requests in memory: v9/v14 keys masked; unrelated v8 still hits; archived IDs kept.\\\")\n'\"","aggregated_output":"Confirmed on 3 real archived requests in memory: v9/v14 keys masked; unrelated v8 still hits; archived IDs kept.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY. Version 3 resolves the sign batching, archive collision and scope findings. Three gaps remain: the serial writer still allows unsafe restarts, the selection record has no durable failure path, and the July transport has no specified guard that stops an unauthorized archive miss before it becomes a paid call.**\n\n## Build blockers\n\n1. **Enforce the serial writer and restart rules.** Table 1 says a second writer and a restart with changed input or configuration are unsupported, but the product entry point still accepts them. Replay routes items before the write savepoint. On restart, dispatch can reuse the old sequence and `round.run` can load the old handover under the new configuration. For example, v119 could commit the July link and a v118 restart could judge the same unfinished day with the v7 renderer. Use the existing store lock at the supported writer entry points and check the unfinished day’s configuration and input identity before dispatch. Allow version switches after a completed day. Specify what happens if a process dies after a provider attempt but before the answer reaches the archive. An unanswered reservation must stay charged, and a restarted sequence must not treat that attempt as free. [Design Table 1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:137) · [Serial replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/replay.py:51) · [Dispatch resume](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/dispatch.py:23) · [Saved handover](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:97) · [Store lock](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:57)\n\n2. **Give selection and write outcomes an append-only record that survives failure.** The new `link_selections` table avoids the preflight and trace grouping problem. The placement after the second match and before `matched` success is correct. A keyword-only `proposed_links=None` preserves the existing writer calls. The remaining gap is at failure: an outcome appended inside a failed write savepoint rolls back, and `round.run` writes the normal `written` notes only after `writing.write` returns successfully. Record the proposal under an attempt ID. Append the committed outcome with the item on success, and append the failed outcome after rollback in the transaction that records the failure. Include a failing Jev request’s computed hash and error. `jev.ask` raises without returning a call ID when validation fails, and a transport failure may leave no archive row at all. [Design §1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:24) · [Writer rollback](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:112) · [Round success and failure paths](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:153) · [Jev failure paths](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:87)\n\n3. **Put the July allow-list in front of the budget transport.** The writable archive design works. I checked three real archived requests in memory: retiring v9 and v14 made their original hashes miss, v8 still hit, and all three retained their call IDs. After a miss, however, `model.call` and `jev.ask` invoke whatever transport they were given. `BudgetTransport` will reserve and send any request it receives within budget. Specify the wrapper that denies every miss except v9/v14 judgements and the selector calls at sequence 148. Assert that the first attempt for each eligible target judgement is fresh. Also stop on a committed out-of-pair reader when the selection is inspected, as the brief says. Waiting for it to miss the archive does not enforce that rule, because a reader without evidence may never be judged. Prove both stop paths with the recording fake before a send. [July test plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:28) · [Archive retirement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:95) · [Lookup and transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:251) · [Budget transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:262) · [Judge eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:300)\n\n## Resolved findings and nonblocking checks\n\n- **Selection and labels.** The two sign builders work with Jev’s single shared candidate state. The prompts ask in the selected reading direction, and the code uses Jev’s returned choice and its probability. The typed order and label calculation work for the July pair, its mirrors and a reversed successor. Tighten the `together` example to state what makes the segment move with the whole, such as a stable mix. Add the remaining cross-industry examples required by §6 and a test with both directions in one sign job. [Design §§2 and 5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:54) · [Jev request shape](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:82) · [AGENTS §6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:226)\n- **Cycles.** Checking every proposed link, correcting the rejected directions, and refusing an item whose corrected graph still cycles follows PRD 06. Refusing unbound waits closes the gap from round 5. Spell out that the checker follows the **effective resolved target** of a stored dependency. Test that a bound legacy wait participates in a cycle check and passes the unbound-wait admission check. Update Table 4 to cite that admission rule. [Design §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:96) · [Stored target resolution](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:235) · [PRD 06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:133)\n- **Judging and the July controls.** The multiline rendering, queue eligibility, comparison-point change cases, v7 controls and fixed-`neither` prefix check answer the prior findings. The July 11 dry run correctly distinguishes a changed total that queues Data Center from a control with no Data Center call. The shared budget plan now describes the Jev retry reservation accurately. Report an overrun or unknown charge using the budget ledger, and keep a ceiling stop before all six sequences finish inconclusive. [Design renderer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:81) · [July dry run](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:9) · [Budget settlement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:153)\n\nThe next revision needs an enforced writer and restart boundary, a durable failure record tied to the selection attempt, and a July transport that denies unapproved misses before reservation. **NOT READY TO BUILD.**"}}
